---
name: grill-me-to-brief
description: Interview the user relentlessly about a plan or design, then write the agreed context brief for the current implementation run.
---

# Grill Me to Brief

Interview me relentlessly about every aspect of this plan until we reach a shared understanding. Walk down each branch of the design tree, resolving dependencies between decisions one by one. For each question, provide your recommended answer.

Ask the questions one at a time.

If a question can be answered by exploring the codebase, explore the codebase instead.

## Output

When the interview is complete, consolidate the result into the context brief using the template at:

`.agents/skills/start-rapid-flow/assets/context-brief-faq-{REQUEST-NAME}.md`

Use the existing run ID; do not create a second run or store the brief outside that run directory. Preserve decisions, rationale, assumptions, unresolved questions, repository evidence, and confidence. Do not turn the brief into a PID, implementation plan, or solution specification.

Do not modify any other file. Verify the file exists and report its path.
